REDUCEME programs that need manual checks
==========================================

These programs use the graphic cursor or graphic buttons, so they cannot
be driven by the automatic regression tests (PGPLOT /NULL device). After
changes that may affect them, run each one by hand with the synthetic data
(python3 tests/mkdata.py DIR) or real data, using an interactive PGPLOT
device, and compare with the behaviour of the reference version (tag 5.1):

- the program starts, plots the data and the buttons respond;
- the main options run without runtime errors;
- output files (if any) are identical to those produced by version 5.1
  with the same answers and cursor actions.

Programs (19). The paths that do not need the cursor of adnhand (up to
its known error), fit2dspl, skysubm and snratio are also covered by the
regression tests.

- adnhand: Create a new spectrum by adding spectra from different images (with interactive monitoring of the S/N ratio).
- cleanest: Automatic and interactive removal of cosmic rays.
- fcalspl: Generates a flux calibration spectrum using splines.
- fcalsplnew: Generates a flux calibration spectrum using splines, allowing an absolute flux calibration.
- fillimage: Fill an image region by extrapolating the signal in a contigous region. The program detects the transition between the extrapolated region and the fitted region as a sudden signal change.
- findarc: Interactive arc line identification.
- fit2dspl: Fits 2-D splines and local polynomials.
- fitdata: Fits polynomials using tabulated data.
- interlines: Interpolates lines in a spectrum by using data from a similar spectrum.
- interpmove: Interpolation/extrapolation of data in an image by using polynomials around a previously fitted polynomial.
- leeposs: Reads FITS images created with getimage from the Digital Sky Survey, allowing the determination of accurate coordinates and plotting of marks.
- midelines: Measures lines (EW) in a spectrum selecting regions manually.
- multfit: perform simultaneous fits.
- plots: General program to produce line plots and display images.
- plotsp3d: Plots successive spectra with a 3-D perspective.
- skysubm: Calculates and subtracts a sky image by fitting polynomials to each channel.
- snratio: Determines the S/N ratio as a function of binning in the spatial direction.
- testwc: Test the wavelength calibration by measuring the positions of sky lines.
- vaucoul: Fits a de Vaucouleurs profile to a galaxy frame. With the previous fit, the program also computes a Sersic profile.
